def novelty_table(title, headers, rows, widths):
    cap=Paragraph(title,styles['tablecap'])
    data=[[Paragraph(escape(v),styles['headcell']) for v in headers]]
    data.extend([[Paragraph(escape(v),styles['cell']) for v in row] for row in rows])
    t=Table(data,colWidths=[CW*w for w in widths],repeatRows=1,hAlign='CENTER')
    t.setStyle(TableStyle([('GRID',(0,0),(-1,-1),.55,colors.black),('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,-1),colors.white),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'MIDDLE'),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),6),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5)]))
    story.extend([cap,t,Spacer(1,9)])

chapter('Novelty and Original Contribution')
p('<b>Contribution statement.</b> SpillGuard contributes a Windows-focused diagnostic workflow that connects process-level GPU-memory observations to controlled local-LLM slowdown experiments, validated remedies and replayable evidence inside an interactive OS laboratory. Its originality is supported as an implemented systems integration and a measured diagnostic case study. The evidence does not establish a first-ever spill detector, a new scheduling algorithm or universal research priority.')
h('N1 From a pressure alert to a validated incident')
p('A high memory counter describes pressure, but does not establish how much useful work has slowed. SpillGuard Repro freezes the model, prompt, context and output work; runs baseline, pressure and recovery; checks output hashes and observed manipulation; and records PASS, FAIL or INCONCLUSIVE. This turns an alert into a testable incident record. Causal profiling and counterfactual debugging are established [20, 21]; the project contribution is their limited experimental adaptation to owned co-tenant activity in the Windows local-inference workflow. [9, 12]')
h('N2 Keeping allocation while changing activity')
p('The retained pilot shows comparable displayed memory counters with a 2.37-times slowdown for an active co-tenant and approximately 1.03 times baseline for an idle co-tenant. A subsequent remedy retained the 3,709 MiB allocation while pausing activity, producing ratios of approximately 1.01 in two matched trials. This demonstrates why occupancy and harmful interference must be distinguished in this workload. It is an empirical contribution of this implementation and dataset; first discovery of the general phenomenon is not claimed. [9, 11, 26]')
h('N3 Connecting resource safety to native observation')
p('The platform places simulated paging, resource matrices and process dispatch alongside live or recorded host memory. Its admission view compares textbook Banker completion assumptions with reservations for long-lived applications. Python and browser implementations expose this reasoning during replay. The reservation is a context-specific adaptation of established resource-allocation principles, not a new safety theorem. The educational contribution is the inspectable connection from an OS concept to a native memory decision; learning gains have not yet been measured. [1, 6, 7, 25]')
p('<b>Defensible novelty claim.</b> The project combines an OS teaching environment with an evidence-preserving Windows GPU-memory diagnosis workflow and demonstrates a local case where changing co-tenant activity restores inference performance without freeing its allocation. This is a concrete project contribution. Superiority over existing profilers and global uniqueness remain unestablished.')

chapter('Novelty Comparison with Existing Work')
p('This comparison identifies established capabilities before stating the project difference. Papers are compared by their described contributions; official tool documentation establishes available features. No competitor was executed under a matched benchmark. A different platform or interface alone is insufficient to establish research novelty.')
novelty_table('Comparison N1  Closest published methods and documented tools',['Existing work','Already established','SpillGuard distinction and limit'],[
('Nsight [14]; hypomnesis [15]; VGPU-Mon [27]','Windows paging timelines, saturation/shared-growth detection and per-process GPU telemetry.','Adds frozen-work records, owned remedy trials and OS-lab replay. Monitoring and the detector principle are not new.'),
('PILOT [16]; Nixie [17]','Oversubscription mitigation using memory-aware scheduling; transparent consumer-GPU multiplexing.','Diagnoses an unchanged target rather than replacing GPU scheduling. Pausing and serializing competing work are established remedies.'),
('CONCUR [18]; PagedAttention [23]','KV-pressure-aware admission and efficient KV-cache management.','Explains host VRAM/commit reservations and long-lived claims. It does not invent KV paging or establish a new admission policy.'),
('DrGPUM [19]','Attributes memory inefficiencies to objects and APIs and guides optimization.','Uses process-level intervention and recovery rather than object profiling. Greater diagnostic precision is not demonstrated.'),
('Coz [20]; CADET [21]','Performance interventions, causal profiling and counterfactual diagnosis and repairs.','Adapts controlled activity changes to Windows inference. It does not invent causal diagnosis or verify a residency mechanism.'),
('GGUF Parser [22]','Estimates memory with context, layer offload and runtime-related configuration.','Adds local calibration and observed-holder admission context. The weights-plus-KV-plus-buffer decomposition is established.'),
('Delta debugging [5]; ProbDD [24]','Input reduction while preserving a property, with informed candidate selection.','Implements bounded transforms and proxy checks. Real-witness reduction benefit and global minimality remain unproven.'),
('Buck and Perugini [25]','Interactive OS scheduling simulation through a React web application.','Connects the simulator to native GPU diagnostics and evidence replay. React, Gantt charts and visualization are established.')
],[.25,.33,.42])
p('<b>Assessment.</b> The supported originality lies in the implemented diagnostic task and its evaluated local example. The reviewed sources do not establish that the exact integration is globally unique. Living tool documentation is compared as accessed on 24 October 2026; feature-level priority dates were not independently audited.')

