h('Why the empirical distinction matters')
p('On nine valid dose/idle trials, the original counter detector alerted on all four severe failures and on three of five non-failures: precision was 4/7 for this severe-slowdown label. The contribution is not perfect detection. Matched experiments supply information that the counter alert lacks, while recovery and fixed-work checks strengthen the incident record. The active/idle contrast motivates residency-event verification; it does not itself prove repeated page migration. [9, 11, 26]')
h('Research scope and stronger validation')
p('The targeted review screened 42 search-result candidates across six searches covering Windows diagnostics, GPU scheduling, causal diagnosis, reduction, model estimation and OS simulators. Selected primary manuscripts, author abstracts and official documentation support the comparisons [14–27]. This is not an exhaustive proof that no identical system exists. External literature establishes what is already known; the project experiments establish its own results.')
p('A stronger publication-level claim requires matched diagnostic-baseline comparisons, more models and hardware, independent residency measurements, and reducer evaluation on the real positive witness under equal budgets. Current evidence supports a distinctive engineering integration and bounded empirical finding. It does not establish a globally first detector, a novel general-purpose algorithm, patentability or unmeasured superiority.')
